; The fidelity scorer (4.5b). It decides the headline number, so both failure
; directions are pinned: too strict punishes an arbitrary stem choice, too
; loose lets a converted A-form score as correct.

(test
 (name test_score)
 (modules test_score)
 (libraries tfl bench test_support))

; The back-check (4.4), offline half. The first test decides whether the
; mechanism can work at all: if a meaning-inverting formula renders into the
; same English as the correct one, no judge could ever catch it.

(test
 (name test_backcheck)
 (modules test_backcheck)
 (libraries tfl tfl_verify translate test_support))

; The anaphora resolution policy (5.2). Pratt-Hartmann Thm 15/16: restricted
; anaphora is NEXPTIME-complete and general anaphora is UNDECIDABLE on the
; same syntax — so the paper's "our fragment is decidable" sentence turns on
; which policy the engine implements. It implements neither: a primed name is
; a constant. Negatives are carried by exhibited countermodels, because the
; engine answers Unknown outside the categorical fragment.

(test
 (name test_anaphora)
 (modules test_anaphora)
 (libraries tfl tfl_verify test_support))

